WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.503
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Lena Dunham.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.738
So, this is a film.
You adapted it.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.206
You also directed it.

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:10.209
It's been a while since you've
been in the director's chair.

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.311
I know it got rave reviews
in Toronto.

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:15.015
But was it exciting to get
behind the camera again?

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.416
-Yeah, it's my favorite place
to be.

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.085
It's my most favorite place
to be.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.620
It's like that cheesy feeling
where you're like,

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.090
"Oh, I'm doing the thing that
I was brought here to do."

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.659
And it's adapting my favorite
book from when I was

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:30.463
10 years old, so I'm living all
kinds of fantasies come true.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.731
And I got to move through
the medieval times

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:35.368
and basically experience
"Back to the Future"

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.504
but reverse but forward?
-It's funny because --

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.874
you know, I think of "Girls" as
this like, again, quintessential

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:44.644
New York show in the same way I
think of you as this sort of

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.980
quintessential New York,
you know, personality.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.349
And here you are in London

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:53.019
and you make a film with
a very stacked British cast.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:55.221
Did you find it
to be a departure?

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.956
Did you find them different
to direct at all?

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.191
-I love English actors.

00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:01.928
Listen, I love all actors.
I respect what they do.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.396
I worship every cast
I work with.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.831
But I will tell you, like,
America around actors

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.967
is a little bit of
like a cult of personality.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.303
It's about like showing up with
the cool 'tude.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.305
And I would say in England,
it's --

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.141
I can't believe I just said
'tude like a 97-year-old man.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.342
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.811
-But in England it's more
like a cult of craft.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.080
Like, those British actors,
like, it's not like,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.249
"Oh, I think I'll learn my lines
in the hair and makeup chair,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.684
let's play around."
They are not coming to play.

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:27.620
It's a military operation.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.824
Like, you do not show up not
knowing what you're going to do

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.759
when you have a cast of people

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.261
who have been in
"Game of Thrones."

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.629
-Yeah.
-They're not --

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.231
-You had a lot of "Throne"-ers
in the show.

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:42.869
If people noticed in the clip,
we had -- which was --

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.137
It actually took me a minute
when I started watching this.

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:46.606
So that's your star.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.675
-Bella Ramsey,
a.k.a. Lyanna Mormont.

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.643
-Yeah, Lyanna Mormont.
And I feel like we never

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:53.479
got to see -- You certainly show
us a lot more range

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.181
than she ever got
to show on "Game of Thrones."

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.315
-Well, yes. This was --

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.251
-Not a lot of comedy
from Lyanna Mormont.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.652
-I believe my dad's quote was,

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.754
"You cast that
tiny scary person."

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.323
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.824
And then he asked, "Did she give
you a lot of 'tude?"

00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:07.226
[ Laughter ]
-That's exactly --

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:09.562
-Because he was of the age
that you used 'tude.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.631
-And I will say
that she is lovely,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:15.100
gave me zero 'tude,
and is a complete genius.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.103
So yeah, we got her.
-Uh-huh.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.371
And then three more
"Thrones"-ers

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:20.940
at least, I counted.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.343
So that is --
Let me get this right.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.879
That's that tiny guy
who jumped off the thing.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:28.915
-Yeah, yeah. Right.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.583
-I just watched once through,
you guys.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.718
I loved it,
but it's very intense.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.254
-Yeah. Tommen.

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.721
-Yes, Tommen.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.890
-Little Prince Tommen.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.827
-This gentleman
has a very important --

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.162
all of the names are --
like, I could make up a

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.864
"Game of Thrones" name for him.
-Do it.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:48.534
-His name is
Vandrik Katarsavie.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.669
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:52.304
-Katarsavie, yes.
Of the Katarsavies.

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:53.540
-Of the Katarsavies.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.641
-Their crest was
a crab holding a sword.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.243
-That's exactly right.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.445
Of the crab-sword-holding
Katarsavies.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:03.416 line:0%
And then that is, I mean,
British legend David Bradley.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:07.720 line:0%
And if you have not seen David
Bradley in full knight's armor

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.822 line:0%
looking for a Wi-Fi signal,
then you have not lived.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.658 line:0%
-Oh, that's great.
-Just walking around base camp.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:15.561
[ Laughter ]
Clanking around.

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.196
-And that's Walder.
I remember that one.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:20.232
He's Walder.
-And then also Ralph Ineson,

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:24.170
who I believe plays --
well, I know that he --

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:29.175
his last name
in it is...Kratolanium.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.309
No, I don't know.
I can't remember.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:33.179
But Ralph Ineson is
another "Thrones"-er

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.447
who was in our cast.
-And it must have also --

00:03:35.447 --> 00:03:40.285
I mean, to do a period piece
film in England is just

00:03:40.285 --> 00:03:42.354
one more added wonderful
element.

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:44.022
-I just have to say,
like, you just stand there

00:03:44.022 --> 00:03:46.125
and you're like, "As a New York
Jewess, this is not

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.526
where I thought
I would find myself."

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:49.395
[ Laughter ]
"And I feel blessed."

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.631
Like, not a bagel in sight.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.432
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:54.967
But a corset everywhere
you look.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:56.101
-There you go.
-And I love that.

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:58.470
-That is a departure
and we are all lucky

00:03:58.470 --> 00:03:59.538
that you made it on our behalf.

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:00.607
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:02.308
It's always so great.
-Always a joy.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.143
-You guys, that's Lena Dunham.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:07.846
"Catherine Called Birdy" is
in select theaters next Friday

00:04:07.846 --> 00:04:09.582
and on Prime Video October 7th.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.384
We'll be right back with Jo Koy.

